-- ============================================================
-- I-371  Orgrimmar WMO minimap tiles - GEOMETRY-MATCHED to our WMO
-- ============================================================
-- The tile filename encodes a GROUP INDEX, and the index -> geometry mapping
-- differs between builds. Matching our stock 3.3.5 Ogrimmar_NNN.wmo MOGP
-- bounding boxes against Whitemane 15595's: 101 of 145 groups are offset by +1,
-- 22 are unchanged, 2 by +2 (matches within 0.03 yd). So naming a tile by our
-- index and taking Whitemane's file of the same name ships the WRONG ROOM's art
-- for ~103 groups - which is what put a misplaced patch on the minimap in the
-- Grommash Hold screenshot (our 110-114 = Whitemane 109-113).
--
-- These rows ship Whitemane's tile for the group whose BOUNDING BOX matches ours,
-- renamed to our index. Never match these tiles by filename.
--
-- BLPs: zep-legacy/mpq/source-assets/Textures/Minimap/kalimdor/ogrimmar/ (PATCH-Z).
-- Companion: [I-371]_wmoareatable.sql (flags 32 on the top-level row, I-012 route).
-- ============================================================

-- Rows beyond the stock trs: where a mapped source group has a tile our client's
-- trs never listed, the row is ADDED (the client keys on the src path it derives
-- from the group, so a new row renders - same as I-303 adding PygmyCave rows).
-- This is what covers Grommash Hold's second room (our group 114 = Whitemane 113).

